                <note rend="inline" type="source">721.23/1014: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-02-06T11:00:00-05:00">February 6, 1933—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 12:05 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>27. My 25, February 4, 3 p.m. Personal for Rublee: Olaya yesterday informed
                    Foreign Affairs Advisory Committee, which includes Lopez and Valencia, of
                    suggestions and also advised Santos at Geneva. Last night Committee submitted
                    report unanimously opposing suggestion and insisting that only possible formula
                    is original Brazilian one. This morning he received telegram from Santos in the
                    same sense. Olaya must therefore withdraw acceptance.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
